  "detail": "Factory gates follow a targeted pass with a full-suite retry. Land checks skip that, so the targeted retry is safe only when every failure in the first run is attributed to a listed file. Today it isn't required. Reproductions (Codex, fake land executor): (1) JUnit `<testsuites errors=\"1\"><testsuite file=\"README.md\" failures=\"1\" errors=\"0\"/></testsuites>` with exitCode 1. parseJUnit ignores root counters and accepts unmatched suite-level counts, so retrying README.md alone lands the entry. A parent-level error and a well-formed report missing a failing case do the same. (2) exitCode 1, a JUnit report attributing one failure to README.md, and output containing `# Unhandled error between tests \u2026 1 error`. The targeted pass lands; a load-error variant also lands. Fix: allow the land retry only when attribution is complete. Every failure and error counter at every JUnit level must be matched by failing test cases in the listed files, and the runner's own summary must agree, with no unhandled errors, load errors or extra error count. When completeness can't be established, block as today. Keep the factory gates' behaviour unchanged. Test each reproduction."
